    summary: "Blasts reported in Yemen's Houthi-held Hodeidah, while government forces attack positions south of Taiz Al Jazeera reports, citing local sources, that blasts have been heard in western Yemen's Houthi-controlled Hodeidah. The Saudi-led coaltion had recently renewed strikes on Houthi targets at the city's port, which sits on the Red Sea coast. Meanwhile, Yemeni government forces claimed attacks on Houthi positions south of Taiz, in the country's southwest. The government-run Saba news agency reported that Houthi shelling of the city killed a woman and wounded at least seven others, including a child.",
