    title: "Trump and NATO chief urge Russia to avoid actions that widen Ukraine war",
    summary: "The message comes after the U.S. leader met Russian President Vladimir Putin last week in Asia, referring to him as a \"friend.\"",
    preview: "WASHINGTON – Russia should avoid actions that expand its war in Ukraine, U.S. President Donald Trump and NATO chief Mark Rutte said in a joint statement on Wednesday after a meeting in Florida where they also discussed the Iran war. The meeting came after the Republican leader, who has been critical of America’s Western allies, met Russian President Vladimir Putin and Chinese leader Xi Jinping last week in Asia, referring to each as his “friend.” “We also discussed the importance of Russia avoiding any actions that intentionally, or unintentionally…",
    body: "WASHINGTON – Russia should avoid actions that expand its war in Ukraine, U.S. President Donald Trump and NATO chief Mark Rutte said in a joint statement on Wednesday after a meeting in Florida where they also discussed the Iran war.\n\nThe meeting came after the Republican leader, who has been critical of America’s Western allies, met Russian President Vladimir Putin and Chinese leader Xi Jinping last week in Asia, referring to each as his “friend.”\n\n“We also discussed the importance of Russia avoiding any actions that intentionally, or unintentionally, expand the war, and the importance of obtaining a peaceful resolution to the war as rapidly as possible,” the leaders said in their statement.\n\nTrump’s meeting with Putin triggered a backlash from domestic Democratic opponents and European allies, with the latter having pushed to be included in U.S.-backed talks to end the war in Ukraine.\n\nRutte, who has repeatedly tried to soothe tension within NATO and keep Trump onside, has said it was normal for major nuclear powers to meet.\n\nRutte and Trump also talked about boosting defense spending and investment in the United States and across NATO, according to their statement.\n\nThe war in Ukraine and U.S.-Israeli war on Iran were the primary subjects of the talks, it added, but did not say what was discussed on Iran.\n\nUkrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy, who has been criticized by Trump, has said Europe had to be included in peace talks.\n\nTrump has often criticized Washington’s Western and democratic allies over issues such as NATO spending, trade tariffs and what he calls their inadequate support for the war on Iran.",
