    title: "U.S. officials divided over China spying allegations after Jensen Huang’s return",
    summary: "A central question remains unanswered: Was the woman Huang was having an affair with a Chinese spy?",
    preview: "Days after U.S. President Donald Trump declared Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang not a security threat to the United States, a central question remains unanswered: Was the woman Huang was having an affair with a Chinese spy? Senior U.S. national security officials, including at the White House, FBI and the CIA, have debated that question in recent days in an effort to determine if Alice Huang — a former executive at a major Nvidia customer — was working for or passing information to China’s premier spy agency, according to five people familiar with the matter…",
    body: "Days after U.S. President Donald Trump declared Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang not a security threat to the United States, a central question remains unanswered: Was the woman Huang was having an affair with a Chinese spy?\n\nSenior U.S. national security officials, including at the White House, FBI and the CIA, have debated that question in recent days in an effort to determine if Alice Huang — a former executive at a major Nvidia customer — was working for or passing information to China’s premier spy agency, according to five people familiar with the matter, who spoke on the condition of anonymity.\n\nThe U.S. has collected intelligence on Alice Huang and her contact with individuals associated with China’s Ministry of State Security (MSS), said two of the people, who were briefed on the intelligence. That intelligence has been described for months in reports from several intelligence agencies, including the CIA, the people said.",
